;; A death test: a pattern with an embedded NUL is refused by name, not
;; silently truncated into a different pattern that matches the wrong
;; thing. The same refusal covers match-re's subject, open-file's path and
;; mode, remove-file's path, and execute's argv -- every boundary whose
;; C string would stop at the NUL and behave as if the rest had never
;; been there.
(compile-re "a\0b")
(print "not reached")
